---
// The weights of one time, under a slider: the Theory page's figure.
---
<figure class="weights" id="weights">
  <div data-timeline></div>
  <div data-chart class="chart"></div>
  <p data-note class="note-line">&nbsp;</p>
  <figcaption>
    <b>The fourteen weights of one time.</b> Each bar is the weight of one
    elastic solve in the displacement at the time on the slider; the vertical
    line marks that time among the states. A state much slower than the time
    carries almost nothing. The others alternate in sign and are each far
    larger than their sum, which is always one. At the earthquake itself the
    elastic state stands alone.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
  import { startWeights } from "../viz/weights";
  startWeights(document.getElementById("weights")!, import.meta.env.BASE_URL);
</script>
